.TH SOON 1 "November 2026" "soon 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soon \- keyboard-driven agenda and todo TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soon
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ DATE ]
.br
.B soon quick
.IR TEXT ...\&
|
.I FILE
| \-
.br
.B soon export
.BR org | ics | vcf
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B soon import
.BR org | ics | vcf
.I FILE
.br
.B soon config
.br
.B soon manual
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soon
is a calendar and todo manager for the terminal. It keeps events, todos,
places, a location timeline and a contact list in plain UTF-8 text files,
shows them in year, three-month, month, week and day views, and is driven
entirely from the keyboard. It depends on nothing but the C library.
.PP
Without arguments it opens the interface on today. With a
.I DATE
it opens on that day; the date can be written in any of the forms the
.B g
command accepts (see
.BR "GO TO A DATE" ).
When standard output is not a terminal, as in
.BR "soon | head" ,
it prints what is coming up instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE"
Agenda file. Default:
.BR $SOON_FILE ,
else
.IR ~/.local/share/soon/agenda.soon .
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE"
Contacts file. Default:
.BR $SOON_CONTACTS ,
else
.I contacts.soon
next to the agenda file.
.TP
.BI \-C " FILE"
Configuration file. Default:
.BR $SOON_CONFIG ,
else
.IR ~/.config/soon/config .
.TP
.BI \-s " SLOT"
Minutes per slot in the week and day views: 5, 10, 15, 30 or 60
(default 15).
.TP
.B \-a
ASCII glyphs only; no box-drawing or marker characters.
.TP
.B \-m
Start without the key menu at the bottom
.RB ( M
toggles it).
.TP
.B \-p
Print what is coming up instead of opening the interface.
.TP
.BI \-d " DAYS"
How far ahead
.B \-p
looks (default 7).
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-h
Print a usage summary.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "quick " TEXT ...
Add one item written as a single line (see
.BR "QUICK CAPTURE" ).
With a single argument naming a readable file, or
.BR \- ,
read one item per line from that file or from standard input; blank lines
and lines starting with
.B "# "
are skipped. Each added item is echoed; lines that cannot be read are
reported on standard error and the exit status is 1.
.TP
.BI "export " "org|ics|vcf " [ FILE ]
Write the agenda as org-mode or iCalendar, or the contacts as vCard, to
.I FILE
or standard output.
.TP
.BI "import " "org|ics|vcf FILE"
Merge items or contacts from a file
.RB ( \-
for standard input). Existing entries are updated by identity; nothing is
deleted.
.TP
.B config
Print a commented default configuration file. Redirect it to
.I ~/.config/soon/config
to start customizing.
.TP
.B manual
Show this manual page, whether or not
.B soon
is installed: the page is looked for next to the executable (a source
checkout) and under the installation prefix.
.SH KEYS
The views nest: year, three months, month, week, day. The agenda panel
under the calendar lists the cursor day's items, its open todos and what
is coming soon.
.SS Moving
.TP
.BR "h j k l" ", arrows"
Move by day; by time slot in the week and day views.
.TP
.BR "." ", " t
Today.
.TP
.BR "[ ]" "   " "{ }" "   " "( )"
Back and forward a week, a month, a year.
.TP
.BR + ", Enter   " \- ", Backspace"
Zoom in and out through the views.
.TP
.BR "n p" ", PgDn PgUp"
Next and previous period of the current view.
.TP
.B g
Go to a date (see
.BR "GO TO A DATE" ).
.TP
.B Tab
Into the day's items:
.B j/k
move,
.B Enter
edits,
.B Esc
leaves.
.SS Items
.TP
.B o
Quick add: a one-line prompt that stays open for the next line until an
empty line or
.BR Esc .
.TP
.B O
Bulk add: opens
.B $VISUAL
or
.B $EDITOR
on a buffer with the grammar as comments, one item per line. Lines that
cannot be read come back once for fixing.
.TP
.BR a ", " T
New event, new todo, through a form.
.TP
.BR e " " x " " m " " d
Edit, mark done, move, delete the selected item. Deleting one occurrence
of a repeating item asks whether to skip only that occurrence.
.TP
.B #
Filter every view down to one tag. Press again and clear the field
.RB ( Ctrl-U )
to remove the filter. The title bar shows the active tag.
.TP
.B A
Upcoming: open todos in deadline order, then every occurrence for the year
ahead, as one list. With a filter active this is the long view of one
area of life.
.TP
.B /
Search items and contacts;
.B Enter
jumps to the hit. Search ignores the tag filter.
.SS Places and sheets
.TP
.B s
Sun and twilight panel for the day's location.
.TP
.BR L ", " H
Location for a range of days; home location.
.TP
.BR v ", " V
Cycle through the sheets: days (slots by days), locations by date, todos,
events, places, contacts. Arrows move,
.B Enter
edits or creates,
.B a
adds a row.
.TP
.B C
The contacts sheet directly.
.TP
.B z
Cycle the slot size: 5, 10, 15, 30, 60 minutes.
.SS Program
.TP
.BR w " " q " " Q
Save; save and quit; quit without saving.
.TP
.B M
Show or hide the key menu.
.TP
.BR ? ", " Esc
Help; close a panel or deselect.
.SH FORMS
.B Enter
confirms a field and moves to the next; on the last field it saves.
.B Ctrl-S
saves from anywhere, and so does
.B Ctrl-Enter
on terminals that can send it (xterm, VTE, kitty, foot, WezTerm; not
Terminal.app).
.B Esc
cancels. Up and down move between fields wherever a field does not need
the vertical arrows itself; the date calendar, the time and duration
strips and the pick lists do, so
.B Tab
and
.B Shift-Tab
always work.
.PP
On a date field the arrows walk a calendar,
.B n/p
move a month,
.B t
or
.B .
is today,
.B \-
clears an optional date. Time fields take typed digits or
.B n
for now; durations take presets or
.B 1h30
typed. The Tags pane lists every known tag (the
.B tags:
line of the configuration plus every tag in use):
.B up/down
pick, the right arrow adds or removes the highlighted one, typing narrows,
and new words simply become new tags.
.SH QUICK CAPTURE
.BR o ,
.B O
and
.B soon quick
share one grammar: one line is one item. Bare words become the title;
everything else is recognized in any order.
.TP
.BR 14:30 ", " 9:30\-9:45
A time (24h) makes the line an event; the default duration is an hour, a
range sets it.
.TP
.BR thu ", " tomorrow ", " 5.11. ", " "sep 14" ", " "next fri" ", " eom ", " +3
A date, in any form
.B g
understands; the longest match wins and only the first date counts.
.TP
.BI due: DATE
A todo deadline, as one compact token
.RB ( due:5.11 ", " due:eom ", " due:fri ).
.TP
.BI # tag
A tag; any number of them.
.TP
.BI @ place
.RB "A place; " @"Duluth\ GA" " for several words."
.TP
.BI & who
.RB "A contact; " &"Simon\ Podnar" " likewise."
.TP
.BR !1 " .. " !5
Priority, todos only.
.TP
.BR +45m ", " +1h30
Duration; it needs a unit, so
.B +2
is a date two days ahead.
.TP
.B *
An all-day event instead of a todo.
.TP
.BI every " rule"
A repeat:
.BR "every mon wed" ,
.BR "every weekdays" ,
.BR "every 2 weeks until 20.12" ,
.BR "every day" ,
.BR "every monthly" .
The rule runs to the next sigiled token or the end of the line.
.PP
Quoted words always stay in the title, so
.B \(dqFish fri\(dq sat
is a todo titled
.I Fish fri
on Saturday. Lone integers are never read as dates:
.I Chapter 14 notes
is one undated todo. A time without a date means today; a repeat without
a date starts today.
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Dentist cleaning thu 14:30 +45m @Clinic #medical
Renew car insurance due:5.11 !2 #financial #car
Standup mon 9:30\-9:45 every weekdays
Pay HOA due:eom every monthly #financial
Call Simon #family
.fi
.RE
.SH GO TO A DATE
The
.B g
prompt, the
.I DATE
argument and every date in the quick grammar accept, case-insensitively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
t today    tom tomorrow    yes yesterday
+3  +3d  \-2w  +1m  \-1y              relative to today
2026\-09\-14  2026\-09  2026           ISO date, month, year
14.9.  14.9.2026   9/14  9/14/2026    European and US forms
sep  september   sep 14   14 sep 2026
mon .. sun   next fri   last fri
next week   next month   last year
w38   w38 2027   2027\-w38             Monday of an ISO week
bom  eom  boy  eoy                    first and last day of month, year
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/soon/config
is a plain
.B key: value
file;
.B soon config
prints a commented default. Keys:
.TP
.B slot
Minutes per slot in the week and day views.
.TP
.B sheet_slot
Minutes per slot in the days sheet.
.TP
.BR work_start ", " work_end
Working hours; the views start there and rows outside are dimmed.
.TP
.B first_weekday
.BR monday ", " sunday " or " saturday .
Week numbers stay ISO.
.TP
.B due_soon
Days ahead within which a todo with a due date is shown as due soon.
.TP
.B tags
Predefined tags, space-separated, offered in the Tags pane and the
.B #
filter alongside the tags already in use.
.TP
.B menu
.BR on " or " off :
the key menu at the bottom.
.TP
.B unicode
.BR auto ", " on " or " off :
box and marker glyphs.
.TP
.B palette
.BR default " or " mono .
.TP
.BI "color " role
Per-role colour:
.IR "fg [on bg] [bold] [dim] [underline] [inverse] [italic]" .
Roles: cursor today busy busier event eventsel allday todo overdue
duesoon tododone sel box panel err now field focus rule titlebar.
The defaults are deutan-safe (blue, yellow, magenta, cyan; never red
against green). Terminals without italics can use
.B "color duesoon: bright\-yellow underline"
instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soon/agenda.soon
Events, todos, places and the location timeline. The format is
documented in
.IR FORMAT.md .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soon/contacts.soon
Contacts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/soon/config
Configuration.
.PP
All three are plain UTF-8 text and safe to edit by hand or keep under
version control. Saves are atomic (written to a temporary file and
renamed).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SOON_FILE ", " SOON_CONTACTS ", " SOON_CONFIG
Override the three file locations.
.TP
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Respected for the defaults.
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
The editor used by
.BR O ;
.B vi
when both are unset.
.TP
.B TZ
Consulted on first run to pick a home location when the agenda has none.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when a file cannot be read or written or when
.B quick
could not read every line; 2 for a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B soon
Open on today.
.TP
.B soon next mon
Open on Monday of next week.
.TP
.B soon \-p \-d 14
Print the next two weeks.
.TP
.B soon quick Dentist thu 14:30 '#medical'
Add an event from the shell. Quote the tag, or the shell drops it as a
comment.
.TP
.B echo 'Call Simon #family' | soon quick \-
The same from a pipe.
.TP
.B soon export ics > agenda.ics
Hand the agenda to another calendar.
